WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.852
Numeric variables can also be classified by how the values are generated.

00:00:04.852 --> 00:00:09.257
Discrete variables usually come from counting events or units.

00:00:09.257 --> 00:00:15.467
Continuous variables come from measurement and conceptually can take values along a range.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.612
Do not confuse the stored precision with the concept.

00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:24.507
A device may report a continuous physiological measurement as a whole number because that is how the

00:00:24.507 --> 00:00:27.202
instrument records it.

00:00:27.202 --> 00:00:33.852
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:38.927
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:46.832
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:48.311
floating-point number.
